### Title
Configuration reference page renders and links correctly.

### Why
The configuration page is now generated by a Sphinx extension; layout, anchors, and cross-references cannot be fully checked by pytest.

### Platforms
- [x] Windows
- [x] macOS
- [x] Linux

### Prerequisites
A docs build (`make -C docs html`) or the Read the Docs preview.

### Steps
1. Open `configuration.html`.
2. Check that each category has a summary table and that every table row links to its entry.
3. Open an entry with aliases (`envs_dirs`) and one that is a map (`custom_channels`); confirm the aliases, environment variables, delimiter, and "not supported" text.
4. Confirm `experimental` and `report_errors` are listed last in their category with a deprecation notice.
5. Check narrow width, dark mode, and JavaScript disabled.
6. Follow the links from the "Configuration" index and `.condarc` pages to the reference.

### Pass criteria
All entries and tables render, permalinks jump to the right entry, and the sidebar lists every setting.

### Out of scope / notes
Content accuracy is covered by `tests/docs/test_config_reference.py`.
